{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage","id":1456310,"title":"The Dream Factory: Los Angeles And The Entertainment Industry In Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-07T13:04:36-07:00","id":1456310,"title":"The Dream Factory: Los Angeles And The Entertainment Industry In Mage","content":"Over at the wiki, it stated that the Technocratic Union didn't pay significant attention to Los Angeles until the 1990s, which doesn't make much sense to me. I'll explain. <br /> <br /> Feedback, thoughts, questions, and corrections are not just welcome, but invited:<br /> <br /> The entertainment industry is of enormous importance to the Union (especially The Syndicate and NWO), and the lion's share of mass produced entertainment in the world is either filmed in Los Angeles, produced by a Los Angeles company, acted in by people who live in the city and are represented by agencies and agents based there, or is somehow dependent upon Los Angeles money, talent, skill, or representation. That's influence over the eyes, ears, and minds of billions of people who consume that media. Moreover, there are few if any industries in which personal connections and being physically present at the right locations (awards ceremonies, charity events, club openings, and so on) is so pivotal to gaining influence and power, meaning that this operation can't be run from a distant boardroom. Worse, a certain amount of actual fame and publicity is key to success even for non-actors. This would make it necessary for Exceptional and even Enlightened agents to be thick on the ground in order to operate effectively within the milieu. The Union would have to pay attention to the city simply because what takes place there affects so much of the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> Los Angeles is briefly referenced in official material as being a Syndicate city. This strikes me as enormously likely. It's not likely that this is the whole story, though. The NWO would insist on having a say in the media output. Problem: Unlike Syndicate agents, who tend to be able adapt to a flashy, more public lifestyle, the Black Suits tend to prefer working from the shadows. This makes it difficult for them to engage in the high-profile whirlwind of the production side of the business. Solution: Take control of the end product before it hits the market. The Hays Code (and later the MPAA) were concessions forced upon the Syndicate by the NWO. They have agents in the Standards and Practices department of every network to determine what can and cannot go out on the air. They also use entertainment media and demographics-related Procedures to kill interest and buzz in media that may weaken the Consensus, and to push the same for media that enforces it. <br /> <br /> See? It really <i>was</i> a conspiracy that caused your favorite show to be cancelled! <br /> <br /> The Syndicate essentially runs the town. That much is true. They chart the courses of entire careers, raising up entertainers to stratospheric heights often only to send them crashing back down into obscurity and poverty, and do so with what must seem like gleeful abandon to an outside observer. There isn't a single significant studio, talent agency, publicity firm, or management corporation that isn't under their thumb, or at least their enormous influence. Their people are on every board, and in every executive suite, usually at or near the head of the table. Not a single major motion picture is released without their say, and not a trophy is given during awards season until they approve the winner (with the occasional surprise due to Statistical Inevitability). A common complaint among other Conventions in the area regards how many Syndicate agents have &quot;gone native,&quot; living the high life and raking in the profits while ignoring their greater responsibilities to humanity. <br /> <br /> I don't see the Progenitors or<br /> iteration X as taking an enormous interest in the area, but the former could be involved with Cedars-Sinai or Children's Hospital LA. The Void Engineers likely have a presence at JPL and Edwards Air Force Base, but not necessarily a significant one.<br /> <br /> The Traditions are a bit more complicated, as one can rest assured that if there's an occult belief, mystery school, pseudoscientific perspective, fringe philosophy, yogic practice, or meditative path to enlightenment out there, then someone in Los Angeles believes in it. This has the downside of a lack of coherence among the various Council-aligned magi, but the upside that if you don't draw too much attention, you can get away with much more than you could in a city with a less diverse and eccentric population. The official White Wolf supplements say that the Hollow Ones pretty much run the nightlife along the Sunset Strip, which makes sense. CoE enthusiasts have had a huge presence since the founding of the studios, though, and maintain it to this day as a never-ending source of illicit substances for those in the right circles, and invites to the most decadent underground parties. <br /> <br /> The official material puts a combined Dreamspeaker/Akashic chantry somewhere in Santa Monica, but as it doesn't relate to the entertainment industry, it's not relevant to this post. <br /> <br /> A few random thoughts and observations:<br /> \u200b<ul><li>The NWO and Syndicate would probably find themselves working at cross-purposes quite often, with the Syndicate tolerating the eccentric religious and spiritual beliefs of the major stars in order to keep them happy and productive, but the NWO trying to keep said beliefs from becoming overly popular or more mainstream.</li> <li>Another potential source of conflict would be the imposition of the Hays Code, which was a response not just to films with content that didn't pass NWO muster, but also to what the Ivory Tower saw as dangerous examples being set by the stars of the day. The Syndicate would have probably been fine with this until they realized the impact on the bottom line.</li> <li>The Syndicate controls the trade papers and glossy entertainment websites and magazines, but the NWO does a brisk trade in TMZ-style gossip and scandal, and uses it as a weapon against stars who have a reputation for promoting extreme lifestyles or alternative belief systems if they seem to pose a threat.</li> <li>It's interesting that the split of the Etherites from the Technocracy happened at about the same time that movie production started to relocate to Hollywood from New York. It's especially worthy of note that one of the reasons for this move was that Thomas Edison's litigious company had a monopoly on the mechanics of film production, much as the Etherites first grew disenchanted with the Union when they sided with Edison over Tesla.</li> <li>Famous (or infamous, depending) LAPD Chief William H. Parker was definitely at least an Exceptional citizen, and possibly an Enlightened one. Either way, he almost singlehandedly brought the department under the firm control of the NWO in the 1950s, and used his officers to brutally enforce any threat to the Consensus. There's probably at least one special unit patterned after Rathbone's Skeleton Keys, and tasked with hunting down Reality Deviants.</li> <li>There are a number of places in the city where the Consensus may be weaker. Venice Beach is one, but also the Angeles Forest, Skid Row, and at least one club on the Sunset Strip.</li> <li>Supposedly JPL founder Alan Parsons was a committed occultist, and attempted a major ritual to bring the Antichrist into the world with future Dianetics author and Scientology founder L. Ron Hubbard. Someone with better legal representation and no fear of litigation could probably do something interesting with that.</li> </ul>I hope that this hasn't been too much of a wall of text. I'd love to know the thoughts of others when it comes to the entertainment industry as it relates to the Traditions and Conventions, and vice versa. I'm especially curious about how certain aspects could be expressed through game mechanics, or rotes and procedures could be used to navigate the industry. I haven't even gotten into the celebrity aspect, which would require a re-examination of Fame and Influence backgrounds from the ground up, or at least an expansion along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T17:01:17-07:00","id":1456320,"title":"","content":"From about 1930 on Hollywood has been the occult capital of Western Civilization. Theater people had traditionally been highly superstitious in Europe from the 18th century up to WWII. The counter culture brought a rivival of this pattern. <br /> <br /> Add to the European influence, Los Angeles is a Pacific Port in constant contact with Asia and Latin America, both of which had and still have strong occult cultures. Both the American branches of the New Age movement and the Pentecostal Church (which quickly became a worldwide movement) began in LA. Don't ignore Tradition and Disperse influence in LA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T20:18:38-07:00","id":1456329,"title":"","content":"If you were trying to flesh out the Mage inhabitants of Los Angeles and what influence they have, one approach would be to start with criticism of the film industry. If there is a trend, try to imagine which Mages are responsible for that trend. <br /> <br /> Bill Maher has become a frequent critic of Hollywood. <br /> The Debbies: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AK-vrk9R-s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AK-vrk9R-s</a><br /> Superheroes: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cD1e0BNNifk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cD1e0BNNifk</a><br /> <br /> I would also junk what the wiki says about the Technocracy ignoring such an important city for any length of time. <br /> <br /> Iteration X - Time Motion Managers would control the massive flow of goods through the port. <br /> <br /> The drug subculture would involve Cult of Ecstasy and Progenitors - Pharmacopoeists. <br /> <br /> \u200bVirtual Adepts would have IT companies. <br /> <br /> America is a two party political system. Hollywood is a left-wing stronghold. The NWO would want to ensure that it stays that way to maintain the balance of power. <br /> <br /> Syndicate - Media Control owning studios and talent agencies makes perfect sense, but I wouldn't have them own it all. There is branch of the Dreamspeakers that focuses on literature and writing. So, you could have some famous scriptwriters be Dreamspeakers. <br /> <br /> There's a lot of prostitution. The Syndicate would want the revenues. &quot;Seeking Arrangement&quot; hookups are a way for any Mage faction to influence powerful executives through secret affairs. <br /> <br /> A homeless Marauder with a message and some followers. <br /> <br /> A crime-fighting Tradition Cabal.<br /> <br /> I might think of more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T04:14:48-07:00","id":1456343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456320#post1456320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From about 1930 on Hollywood has been the occult capital of Western Civilization. Theater people had traditionally been highly superstitious in Europe from the 18th century up to WWII. The counter culture brought a rivival of this pattern.<br /> <br /> Add to the European influence, Los Angeles is a Pacific Port in constant contact with Asia and Latin America, both of which had and still have strong occult cultures. Both the American branches of the New Age movement and the Pentecostal Church (which quickly became a worldwide movement) began in LA. Don't ignore Tradition and Disperse influence in LA.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The non-Industry aspects of Los Angeles would probably require a series of supplements to go into in any detail, as there are so many different cultures and belief systems here that it boggles the mind (According to the U.S. Census, at least 185 languages are spoken at home in the greater metropolitan area of L.A.). You could have a reason for literally any currently existing Tradition or Craft to have a presence in the city. I have a rough outline of a possible history that I'll go into at some point, but I'd say that the Ecstatics and Hollowers have traditionally had the greatest influence on the culture of the area, with Ecstatics likely claiming Venice Beach as their own, and the Hollowers running the scene on West Hollywood's Sunset Strip (though there's significant overlap, and the two groups traditionally get along quite well with each other). <br /> <br /> Choristers had a significant presence early on, but I suspect that the Technoncracy-led downfall of Sister Aimee Semple MacPherson led to a loss of influence that they never truly recovered from. The Order of Hermes has a small yet consistent following, recruiting largely through classes in &quot;ancient mysteries&quot; and various occult techniques, while the Verbena hold sway over a sizeable neo-pagan scene. Sons of Ether have a presence with fad diets and pseudoscientific health regimens. Akashics would obviously be found in Chinatown and Little Tokyo, but also likely recruit among stunt doubles, stunt coordinators, and personal trainers. Euthanatos? Probably a few on the LAPD who manage to fly under the radar of their NWO-aligned compatriots, but they could come from anywhere. I suspect there's likely a subgroup of them in East L.A. who invoke Santa Muerte.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T05:09:06-07:00","id":1456345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456329#post1456329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were trying to flesh out the Mage inhabitants of Los Angeles and what influence they have, one approach would be to start with criticism of the film industry. If there is a trend, try to imagine which Mages are responsible for that trend.<br /> <br /> Bill Maher has become a frequent critic of Hollywood.<br /> The Debbies: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AK-vrk9R-s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4AK-vrk9R-s</a><br /> Superheroes: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cD1e0BNNifk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cD1e0BNNifk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That's my entire approach to the history, thus my noting how the move to Hollywood coincided with the Sons of Ether splitting from the Union. I think that a couple of Etherites and Difference Engineers saw the enormous potential in the new medium, and fled westward to avoid the influence of Edison's monopoly over the technology. The Edison film of Frankenstein was his sneering response to them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also junk what the wiki says about the Technocracy ignoring such an important city for any length of time. </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's been junked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Iteration X - Time Motion Managers would control the massive flow of goods through the port. </div> </div> </div>Los Angeles also has the largest manufacturing sector of any city in the United States (That surprised me, too!), so there's that as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The drug subculture would involve Cult of Ecstasy and Progenitors - Pharmacopoeists. </div> </div> </div>Progenitors and Iteration X would also be on the forefront of cosmetic surgeries and enhancements, which are nearly ubiquitous in the Industry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bVirtual Adepts would have IT companies. </div> </div> </div>They'd also be found working in CGI animation and special effects departments. Considering how much of the gossip industry has moved online, I can also see them involved in running lurid celebrity gossip blogs in order to spread dirt on the Technocracy's favorite stars. Enough correspondence means that you can essentially be nearly anywhere and observe nearly anything that's happening, and from there, it's just a matter of taking a video and uploading it for all to see. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Syndicate - Media Control owning studios and talent agencies makes perfect sense, but I wouldn't have them own it all. There is branch of the Dreamspeakers that focuses on literature and writing. So, you could have some famous scriptwriters be Dreamspeakers. </div> </div> </div>The Baruti! Yes, there's no doubt that a huge number of them would try to break in. I think you'd see more of them working as independent filmmakers, since it would be important to get the story across in just the right way, and leaving the final cut up to the vision of an unawakened director or Syndicate studio executive would destroy the story, or (worse) give it a different meaning from the one intended.<br /> <br /> I don't think that the Conventions would own ALL of the agencies or studios, but they would either control or have enormous influence over all of the major ones. Smaller studios and talent agencies would likely be beneath their notice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a lot of prostitution. The Syndicate would want the revenues. &quot;Seeking Arrangement&quot; hookups are a way for any Mage faction to influence powerful executives through secret affairs. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, not to mention the significant adult movie industry that still survives and thrives in the San Fernando Valley despite the rise of similar content provided for free online. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A homeless Marauder with a message and some followers.<br /> <br /> A crime-fighting Tradition Cabal.<br /> <br /> I might think of more. </div> </div> </div>I look forward to it! Thanks for the extensive and thoughtful feedback so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T07:27:57-07:00","id":1456348,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve played in two short mini-Chronicles both set in L.A., the first in the film noir period right after World War II and the second (a sequel with some of the same characters) in the early 1960s with the affair between Marilyn Monroe and Jack Kennedy. Both were Mage Chronicles with a lot of Vampire stuff going on in the background (and an actual vampire PC in the second one) and I really liked both of them. I like history anyway and we really had a great ST and I had a lot of fun exploring old Los Angeles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T11:14:27-07:00","id":1456354,"title":"","content":"Okay, I'm getting a rough idea of a history together. I'm focusing on the Technocracy mostly right now due to the relationship between the Syndicate and the NWO defining so much of how I see things developing. We can circle back to the history of the Traditions later, and hopefully I'll find a way to combine it all into a coherent and reasonably succinct whole)<br /> <br /> Going far back, the place that would become Los Angeles was likely Dreamspeaker and Verbena territory, at least for those mages who allied themselves with the Council at all. The takeover by the Spanish obviously started with the Explorators, who eventually ceded control over the immediate territory to the Cabal of Pure Thought as part of the mission system. The area probably didn't attract significant notice after that other than as a port of trade. The switch from the Spanish to the U.S. government didn't lead to significant change in this regard, as the discovery of major nodes in San Francisco had led to the Gold Rush of '49, and the Union's attention was focused on that region. The dawn of the 20th century changes all of that.<br /> <br /> 1900s: One result of the feelers put out to the Traditions by the Electrodyne Engineers is a friendship and eventual romantic attachment between the artistically inclined Electrodyne Engineer Sophie Auclair and the Orphan and future Hollow One Daphne Miller (these are placeholder names). Chafing at the restrictions placed upon her by the Technocracy's strict control over motion capture technology, Auclair uses her Convention's split from the rest of the Union to provide cover for her flight to Los Angeles, where she can experiment with new techniques away from Edison's overly zealous patent lawyers. Their initial pictures prove enormously popular with the public, though no prints are known to have survived to the present day: By the time the Union realizes that the films being produced in Hollywood use technologies that don't fit with the timetable, they do their best to confiscate every existing reel, but the damage has been done. The Syndicate moves in to reassert control over the technology.<br /> <br /> 1910s: Other filmmakers take advantage of the mild weather and distance from New York to set up their own operations, with the first official Los Angeles studio being founded by the Syndicate in 1915. <br /> <br /> Auclair and Miller eventually find themselves shut out from the industry created around them by the Syndicate, but remain enormously influential within the Los Angeles social scene, and mentor many up-and-coming actors, directors, and screenwriters. By 1917, the NWO has a presence, but the Ivory Tower hasn't fully caught on to the impact of this technology on the masses. The following decade changes all of this. The Cult of Ecstasy also establishes a strong presence at this time, helping to ensure a steady supply of untainted alcohol to the film community of Hollywood during the dark days of Prohibition.<br /> <br /> The first Nephandic caul known in this area is established at around this time.<br /> <br /> Late in the decade, Aimee Semple McPherson of the Celestial Chorus brings her ministry to the city, and gains immediate and immense support among the masses.<br /> <br /> 1920s: Hollywood begins to gain a reputation for decadence. The NWO tries to bring them into line through public shaming in the national newspapers and film magazines, but this only adds to the mystique. The highly publicized trial of Fatty Arbuckle causes enormous public outcry, but leads to little change in the culture. <br /> <br /> To make matters worse for the Union, the Syndicate seems to not be trying to exert any actual creative control over the film output of the industry, meaning that creative types sympathetic to the traditions have been able to push their propaganda across the United States, and even overseas. Things come to a head in 1925, when the Auclair-influenced film The Lost World is released, and the astounding visual effects for the time cause a slight ripple in the Consensus when many viewers believe that they're watching actual dinosaurs filmed for the movie. This is quickly debunked, but the Ivory Tower grows concerned enough to demand action.<br /> <br /> In response to what the NWO sees as the Syndicate brushing off their concerns, they use their agents in pulpits, in radio and print media, and in government offices to denounce the content of the more provocative motion pictures, especially those with a focus on sex, drug use, violence, the occult, and non-Western religious and spiritual beliefs. This meets with growing success among the masses. Writers, directors, and actors influenced by the Traditions begin to find themselves shut out of work.<br /> <br /> The introduction of talking pictures serves as an excuse for the NWO to further their influence over the Industry, causing enormous resentment among Syndicate members who see this as an unnecessary overreach by their colleagues, one that could affect the bottom line. <br /> <br /> In 1926, The Syndicate and the NWO put aside their differences for long enough to destroy the public reputation of Chorister Aimee Semple McPherson, leading to massive disillusionment for her followers, and growing skepticism towards religion in general. The Celestial Chorus never fully recovers its influence in the region. As an unintentional (?) consequence, however, reports of Nephandic activity in the area increase over the upcoming years and decades.<br /> <br /> 1930s: The NWO takes advantage of the Syndicate's weakened influence following the market crash to exert further control over the film industry. This results in the creation of the Motion Picture Production Code in 1930, and its strict imposition in 1934. As a consequence, the mold is set for what is considered &quot;appropriate&quot; entertainment for the masses for decades to come. This is an enormous victory for the Ivory Tower. A Syndicate faction in favor of rapprochement with their NWO colleagues takes over, their disgraced predecessors reassigned to oblivion. <br /> <br /> The renewed congenial relationship between the Conventions means a renewed focus on discrediting the beliefs of the various Traditions in film: Films such as Frankenstein discourage budding scientists from pushing too far beyond the realm of what is thought possible. Substances and practices sacred to Ecstatics and Dreamspeakers are now fodder for lurid exploitation flicks showing innocent young white American boys and girls seduced into addiction and disease. Ritual magicians are portrayed as evil sorcerers, and worst of all is the blatant racial stereotyping that comes into play when Akashic beliefs are spouted by &quot;Oriental&quot; masterminds, all tribal shamans are shown onscreen as violent savages, and the Euthanatoi are reduced to mindless &quot;Thuggee' cultists by Hollywood. Even the Verbena are mocked by the portrayal of the Wicked Witch of the West in The Wizard Of Oz. <br /> <br /> Working together, the NWO and Syndicate create a studio system that controls the lives of their stars to such a degree that even a hint of scandal or impropriety means the end of a career, preferably before it hits the papers. For studio favorites and stars too popular at the box office to simply fire, black-suited &quot;fixers&quot; go out with a mixture of money, implied threats, and limited but effective violence in order to cover for their indiscretions before they're known. In order to satisfy the insatiable appetite of the public for new content, the Pharmacopoeists are brought in as studio doctors to dole out highly experimental stimulants to actors and writers, which in turn leads to more scandals requiring intervention by studio fixers when the this leads to a crisis in addiction, several mental breakdowns, and more than one death from accidental overdose. <br /> <br /> The masses are fed an endless diet of lavish musicals, screwball comedies, mawkish melodrama, and gangster films where the protagonist meets a grisly end, all of which reinforces desired behavior and none of which contradicts the Consensus. Truly, it is the Technocracy's Golden Age as much as it is that of Hollywood. There's some concern over a handful of film buffs becoming a bit too enamored of the bad guys, but by and large, things are exactly where the Union wants them to be. <br /> <br /> 1940s: With the dawn of World War II, of course, the focus changes almost entirely to the defeat of the Nazis. The temporary truce between the Traditions and the Conventions allows a few experimental and even socially subversive anti-fascist works through the cracks, but by and large, the focus is on more of the same stuff that was being done in the 30s, only now with more people in uniform. <br /> <br /> While the end of the war means the end of the truce between the Traditions and the Conventions, it doesn't mean that every personal relationship developed during that time ends as well. In business meetings and at Hollywood parties, a specific way of doing business has developed, and it requires an ability to tolerate the eccentric beliefs of others to a certain degree. Some lines of communication remain open, and when the Virtual Adepts later bolt the Technocracy, a number somehow still manage to find work in the Industry in fields requiring technical expertise and creativity. This doesn't escape the notice of the Ivory Tower, and their reaction is severe: Dozens of the Syndicate's most effective operatives and creative talents in the Industry are targeted by the House Un-American Activities Committee for suspected Communist activities, with their Syndicate handlers subjected to extensive interrogation and occasional reprogramming. Almost simultaneously, the NWO strips control of the LAPD from the Syndicate, placing the Exceptional (possibly Enlightened) NWO uber-loyalist William H. Parker in a place of influence, and making him Chief of Police in 1950. <br /> <br /> 1950s: In a hugely public &quot;anti-corruption&quot; sweep, scores of the Syndicate's agents in the LAPD are reassigned or dismissed from duty. While a level of corruption still exists, Parker's men (and yes, they are all men) occupy all of the most important positions. They proceed to inflict a reign of terror on the local Reality Deviant population and their allies. Minority and immigrant communities find themselves the target of special attention. Local papers blare lurid headlines of drug rings rousted, juvenile delinquents arrested, voodoo cults smashed, and sex orgies busted. <br /> <br /> Worse for the Syndicate, the NWO has established authority over the television airwaves since TVs became available to the general public, meaning that the people ostensibly in charge of creating the programming have no actual say in the content, and are entirely reliant on the dictates of another Convention regardless of what it means for profitability or prosperity. <br /> <br /> [I'm getting a bit drained, so this seems like a good place for me to take a break. I'll write more at a later time and/or date, but invite comments, questions, and so on in the meantime]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T11:36:44-07:00","id":1456356,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m impressed. Your history is really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T12:12:57-07:00","id":1456362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456356#post1456356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m impressed. Your history is really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That's very kind of you to say. I've been thinking about this for a while, since the rise of the film and television industries in the 20th century has been a subject of interest to me for some now, and I was surprised at the lack of existing material on it as it related to Mage, especially the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-08T16:42:22-07:00","id":1456378,"title":"","content":"I ran a Mage chronicle set in LA, starting prior to M20's release but incorporating the idea that the Traditions were heavily on the rebound, with momentum gained by the internet's leveling of the information disseminating play field and the Syndicate's failure to &quot;win&quot; in 2007, and the blowback it created within the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Technos didn't leave LA alone. Rather, there has been a long tug of war between the Technocracy and Traditions from the silent era onward. I think the OP's point on the timing of the Etherites' departure from the Technocracy coinciding with this era is wise, as &quot;mad genius&quot; served as the basis for many silent films (Cabinet of Dr Caligari, A Trip to the Moon, etc), and the Hays Code was certainly an attempt by the Technos to roll back excesses. The NWO practically wrote the script on WW2 era news reels, which continued into the 50s with the Korean War. The Syndicate and NWO collaborated on a lot of feel good films, rolling in the money and putting out conformist messages. One producer of the era, whose name I forget, said &quot;I want width, not depth,&quot; referring to the big screen wide view pictures of the era; I think that a very NWO motto. The advent of TV brought the conformity message to every home that could afford one, and radio was still a thing for those that couldn't.<br /> <br /> But the Technocracy's greatest adversary isn't the Traditions; it's plain old humanity, with all its inventive genius. People <i>want </i>to tell stories, and not just happy, mundane Doris Day/Rock Hudson types of stories. The NWO let a lot of sci-fi ride in the 50s: both to introduce terrifying creatures -- so that the masses would grow to fear the strange and unnatural -- but also to placate the Void Engineers, who wanted to rush space travel into the Consensus. This all worked, but also served to fortify public desire for strange tales, especially among the youth. The Hollywood machine put out movies more efficiently than ever, but as the studio system broke down it became less tractable.<br /> <br /> Then we have the 60s, where the Cultists made increasing social headway, followed by the 70s, with the Virtual Adepts joining the Traditions, disrupting the Technocracy's clamping down on 60s era social mores. The VA's made moves to put movie making into the hands of as many dreamers as possible. You didn't need a studio any more. Home video and pirating tapes became a thing in the 80s, with a lot of <i>weird</i> stuff showing up in the shadowy corners of Reagan conservatism. In the modern day, anyone can make a movie, and while Hollywood is still the home of the international blockbuster, human ingenuity is as much a driving force as Tradition myth introduction and Technocratic restraint.<br /> <br /> I also had a group of old vampires, collectively called the Producers. Being good vampires, they were always well in the background. I don't think a PC even saw one until nearly the end of the chronicle. But they were always there pursuing their abstruse goals. LA is a terrific setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12765-otto-d-fey","name":"Otto D'Fey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T01:45:32-07:00","id":1456396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Otto D'Fey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456378#post1456378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran a Mage chronicle set in LA, starting prior to M20's release but incorporating the idea that the Traditions were heavily on the rebound, with momentum gained by the internet's leveling of the information disseminating play field and the Syndicate's failure to &quot;win&quot; in 2007, and the blowback it created within the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I agree that the Technos didn't leave LA alone. Rather, there has been a long tug of war between the Technocracy and Traditions from the silent era onward. I think the OP's point on the timing of the Etherites' departure from the Technocracy coinciding with this era is wise, as &quot;mad genius&quot; served as the basis for many silent films (Cabinet of Dr Caligari, A Trip to the Moon, etc), and the Hays Code was certainly an attempt by the Technos to roll back excesses. The NWO practically wrote the script on WW2 era news reels, which continued into the 50s with the Korean War. The Syndicate and NWO collaborated on a lot of feel good films, rolling in the money and putting out conformist messages. One producer of the era, whose name I forget, said &quot;I want width, not depth,&quot; referring to the big screen wide view pictures of the era; I think that a very NWO motto. The advent of TV brought the conformity message to every home that could afford one, and radio was still a thing for those that couldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The advent and popularity of television is going to play a huge role in the Syndicate/NWO rivalry as I see it, and the Syndicate's next moves in Hollywood will be partially in response to the NWO's stranglehold over television in the U.S.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the Technocracy's greatest adversary isn't the Traditions; it's plain old humanity, with all its inventive genius. People <i>want </i>to tell stories, and not just happy, mundane Doris Day/Rock Hudson types of stories. The NWO let a lot of sci-fi ride in the 50s: both to introduce terrifying creatures -- so that the masses would grow to fear the strange and unnatural -- but also to placate the Void Engineers, who wanted to rush space travel into the Consensus. This all worked, but also served to fortify public desire for strange tales, especially among the youth. The Hollywood machine put out movies more efficiently than ever, but as the studio system broke down it became less tractable. </div> </div> </div>This is one of the aspects of later Mage editions that I really like: The Technocratic Union is enormously influential, but there's a certain limit to their abilities. I was going to get into the unintended consequences aspect in the 1970s, when the rise of films like The Exorcist, The Omen, and the original The Wicker Man gave rise to a new wave of interest in occult matters despite none of them being particularly pro-magick, but I think that your idea is a better time to introduce the concept, especially as regards what happens later on with the Void Engineers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then we have the 60s, where the Cultists made increasing social headway, followed by the 70s, with the Virtual Adepts joining the Traditions, disrupting the Technocracy's clamping down on 60s era social mores. The VA's made moves to put movie making into the hands of as many dreamers as possible. You didn't need a studio any more. Home video and pirating tapes became a thing in the 80s, with a lot of <i>weird</i> stuff showing up in the shadowy corners of Reagan conservatism. In the modern day, anyone can make a movie, and while Hollywood is still the home of the international blockbuster, human ingenuity is as much a driving force as Tradition myth introduction and Technocratic restraint. </div> </div> </div>The Cultists are going to nearly define L.A. life in the 60s and 70s, and their influence will reach into the 80s before the Just Say No campaign starts (which will itself lead to unintended consequences).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also had a group of old vampires, collectively called the Producers. Being good vampires, they were always well in the background. I don't think a PC even saw one until nearly the end of the chronicle. But they were always there pursuing their abstruse goals. LA is a terrific setting. </div> </div> </div>I always like introducing other aspects of the WoD for a moment, if only to remind the players that they're not the only ones working behind the curtain. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T08:52:34-07:00","id":1456436,"title":"","content":"In Vampire the Masquerade, Southern California through the 20 century was the home of the Anarchist Revolt Vampires. Neither the Camarilla nor the Sabbat had power here. I assume that the particular Vampire politics would make a difference. In the 1990s the area was taken over by the Camarilla (I think) because of an attack by the Cathayan vampires. San Francisco was a stronghold of the Fae throughout the 20th century. But I don't know much of Fae activity during the 1912-1965 period (classic Hollywood). I could easily see several of the small studios, places like Monogram or Republic, being controlled by the Fae. Independent Producers would be the most likely place for either Trad mages or Fae to be involved in the film industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T16:00:53-07:00","id":1456466,"title":"","content":"After I read about Los Angeles in DtF and its influence on Faith I always imagined that the same logic could be transferred to Mage and Changeling since hollywood 'magic' could be said to inspire hope and dreams and other positive emotions in ways that might counteract consensus or banality - making it in a sense a sort of propoganda center for those who favor more magic and fantasy. By extension you could see the pushing of science fiction as an approach by the Technocracy to shape consensus in ways THEY prefer (And to counter whatever Tradition-based propoganda may push.) In an age of streaming and independent content creators it becomes even easier for this kind of 'propoganda' to flourish even outside Hollywood of course, but I've always seen Hollywood (And perhaps California as a whole) as being one of those 'soft spots' in reality where the supernatural can occur more openly than other factions (like the Union) would prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T16:27:33-07:00","id":1456468,"title":"","content":"If you've never read it, I recommend Gary Krist's <i>Mirage Factory: Illusion, Imagination, and the Invention of Los Angeles</i>. It mainly focuses on William Mulholland, DW Griffin, and Aimee Semple McPherson and how they made LA what it was between 1900 and 1930. (Les Standiford's <i>Water to the Angels</i> is also a good look at Mulholland and his aqueduct project.)<br /> Also two biographies about 1940s/50s rocket scientist and occultist Jack Parsons, John Carter's <i>Sex and Rockets</i> and George Pendle's <i>Strange Angel</i>.<br /> And Dave McGowan's <i>Weird Scenes Inside the Canyon</i>, about the Laurel Canyon music scene of the 1960s/70s, including its various occult, cult, political, and covert military connections. (McGowan is something of a conspiracy theorist, but it makes interesting idea fodder for something like Mage.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 08-09-2021, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T09:02:59-07:00","id":1456763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456436#post1456436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Vampire the Masquerade, Southern California through the 20 century was the home of the Anarchist Revolt Vampires. Neither the Camarilla nor the Sabbat had power here. I assume that the particular Vampire politics would make a difference. In the 1990s the area was taken over by the Camarilla (I think) because of an attack by the Cathayan vampires. San Francisco was a stronghold of the Fae throughout the 20th century. But I don't know much of Fae activity during the 1912-1965 period (classic Hollywood). I could easily see several of the small studios, places like Monogram or Republic, being controlled by the Fae. Independent Producers would be the most likely place for either Trad mages or Fae to be involved in the film industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on all of the above. There's a certain amount of information regarding VtM influence on the film industry in Los Angeles By Night and similar supplements, though they don't explore it too extensively. I'm not currently planning on addressing the presence of other supernaturals except in passing, but I am trying to make sure that I don't directly contradict the existent sourcebooks (or at least no more than they contradict each other). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456466#post1456466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After I read about Los Angeles in DtF and its influence on Faith I always imagined that the same logic could be transferred to Mage and Changeling since hollywood 'magic' could be said to inspire hope and dreams and other positive emotions in ways that might counteract consensus or banality - making it in a sense a sort of propoganda center for those who favor more magic and fantasy. By extension you could see the pushing of science fiction as an approach by the Technocracy to shape consensus in ways THEY prefer (And to counter whatever Tradition-based propoganda may push.) In an age of streaming and independent content creators it becomes even easier for this kind of 'propoganda' to flourish even outside Hollywood of course, but I've always seen Hollywood (And perhaps California as a whole) as being one of those 'soft spots' in reality where the supernatural can occur more openly than other factions (like the Union) would prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that idea. It ties in with some thoughts I was having on how popular trends in movies burn themselves out with endless repeats of the same formula leading to diminishing returns, and how the Syndicate could profit two ways from that. It'll start to come up more in the 60s and 70s, and I'll go into more detail once the concept is more fleshed out. I'm also thinking that a LOT of the streaming content revolution was absolutely unplanned, and doesn't fit into their time table, but they are trying to find a way to gain control of the medium from the masses in order to redirect it into reinforcing the consensus. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456468#post1456468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you've never read it, I recommend Gary Krist's <i>Mirage Factory: Illusion, Imagination, and the Invention of Los Angeles</i>. It mainly focuses on William Mulholland, DW Griffin, and Aimee Semple McPherson and how they made LA what it was between 1900 and 1930. (Les Standiford's <i>Water to the Angels</i> is also a good look at Mulholland and his aqueduct project.)<br /> Also two biographies about 1940s/50s rocket scientist and occultist Jack Parsons, John Carter's <i>Sex and Rockets</i> and George Pendle's <i>Strange Angel</i>.<br /> And Dave McGowan's <i>Weird Scenes Inside the Canyon</i>, about the Laurel Canyon music scene of the 1960s/70s, including its various occult, cult, political, and covert military connections. (McGowan is something of a conspiracy theorist, but it makes interesting idea fodder for something like Mage.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read up on a lot of Los Angeles and entertainment history, but not those books in particular. Thanks for the recommendations! I'll look into acquiring them as funds permit. The aqueduct project is a huge part of the history, and I'm a bit annoyed with myself for not including it in my 1900s entry. I'll have to come up with some backstory for it, because if anything reeks of the Technocratic Union's ruthlessness to the masses in the name of their protection, it's that entire scheme. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll be sketching out some ideas next for the rest of the 50s and 60s. It'll touch on the European and Japanese film industries, the rise of television, the Cult of Ecstasy coming to even greater prominence, and a few major historical events. The reaction of the Traditions and the Union to the Manson murders (not the result of the workings of either side, though fingers will be pointed), the Moon landing, and how it all led to the uncontrolled madness of the 70s are the ones that I'm focusing on right now, but you've all given me plenty of new ideas, as well.<br /> <br /> Oh, and the Nephandi will finally put in a significant appearance.<br /> <br /> You've all been quite supportive and helpful, and I appreciate the thoughtful feedback and suggestions I've been getting. My current plan is to take this up to the modern day, and to have a local Syndicate and NWO that put on an appearance of working in perfect harmony, but are in a constant battle for control over the final product, and work to undercut each other behind the scenes. For reasons I'll get into later, The Syndicate will have a largely hands-off policy towards local Reality Deviants, and has even been known to work alongside them to combat mutual threats, though this is done rarely, and never if the NWO has a chance of knowing about it.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to hearing more from all of you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T12:19:41-07:00","id":1456775,"title":"","content":"Something else you might get some mileage out of is Clive Barker's novel Coldheart Canyon, which is set in LA and involves aspects of Hollywood history. Also his film Lord of Illusions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T12:56:52-07:00","id":1456777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1456310-the-dream-factory-los-angeles-and-the-entertainment-industry-in-mage?p=1456775#post1456775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else you might get some mileage out of is Clive Barker's novel Coldheart Canyon, which is set in LA and involves aspects of Hollywood history. Also his film Lord of Illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the first, saw the second. Good general sources of inspiration and mood on both counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25574-heinrich-mentius","name":"Heinrich Mentius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25574_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T18:35:12-07:00","id":1456794,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it. Changelings and Trade Mages would be most likely to hang out with or be Independent Producers. Small quirky films with distinctive points of view often came from that quarter. The films made by these producers rarely made a big splash and largely flew under the radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T00:35:11-07:00","id":1456798,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle, I had the players work to counteract a Mind+Correspondence+Time+Entropy effect that was affecting the people and culture of a given area. Syndicate - Media Control filtered it through a TV series set in the targeted region, provoking all kinds of reactions. They were steering debate over the show's message in a direction that would benefit their extractive industries. A Los Angeles that has Syndicate and NWO in a contest of influence might have Mind effects working on different audiences.<br /> <br /> If you want players in the setting to take interest in historical figures from sixty years ago, you could make a few of them long lived Life Mages who are still focused on the consequence of an event or seeking revenge for something that was done by another famous Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T19:07:04-07:00","id":1456849,"title":"","content":"My own long running impression is that, because of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1195123-world-of-darkness-hold-the-darkness?p=1202020#post1202020\">the World of Darkness's &quot;gothic punk&quot; nature and what it entails</a>, much of the entertainment world - including films - has had a sharp divide between the mainstream &quot;corporate studio&quot; created material and the counterculture of much smaller &quot;independent&quot; creations. While you do see something of this in the real world, in the WoD, it should be - IMO at least - much sharper and more noticeable. The mainstream is very conformist, very polished, and very safe (at least from the point of view of the powers that be), with the caveat that what is considered &quot;conformist&quot; changes from decade to decade, but usually tend to be what the people in power and experts tell you is what is expected and correct. The counterculture, in contrast, is sometimes &quot;dangerous&quot; or &quot;shocking&quot;, is usually very rough around the edges, and tries to rebel against conformity (sometimes mindlessly, sometimes trying to get you to question your own preconceptions, including if your &quot;rebellion&quot; is just another form of conformity). <br /> Exactly how this specifically manifests itself in the World of Darkness and its Hollywood film industry is certainly debatable (and likely has no single correct answer). I tend to skew towards the idea that it's in specific instances. For example, the idea that the original Terminator film was only given a limited released and then quietly suppressed by certain interests, but became an underground cult thing traded around on bootleg VHS copies. (Until almost a decade later, the concept of a scary killer robot enforcing the murderous will of a future AI overlord gets co-opted into a big budget action movie about a heroic robot savior who spouts one-liner catch phrases and has fast food tie ins.) <br /> <br /> Tangently, I offer up my various Ages of Darkness thread musings about different eras of LA/California as possible idea fodder. (Not all of them are Mage specific, but many of them still work for certain aspects of the game.)<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness?p=1391873#post1391873\">In the Valley of Shadow</a> (Vampire &amp; Wraith in LA and the San Fernando Valley, 1945 - 1960)</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness?p=1389749#post1389749\">Dark Skies</a> (Project: Twilight &amp; The Technocracy in the Western US, 1945 - 1970)</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness?p=1385186#post1385186\">California Dreaming'</a> (Mage &amp; Changeling in California, 1960 - 1970)</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness?p=1429818#post1429818\">Sunset People</a> (WoD: Outcasts &amp; Hunters Hunted in LA, 1972 - 1984)</li> <li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness?p=1409677#post1409677\">End of Days</a> (Hunter &amp; Demon in an alternate 1999 LA)</li> </ul><br /> At some point I want to talk about Old California, just because I'm a life long Zorro fan. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T20:03:27-07:00","id":1456852,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=No One of Consequence;n1456849<br /> At some point I want to talk about Old California, just because I'm a life long Zorro fan. <br /> [/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Seconded! <br /> <br /> To my mind Old California would likely be a place where the Order of Reason might have held out longer. The Chorus and the Cabal of Pure Thought would be struggling to control the Church. The Hermetics, always strong in Spain, would dominate secular Mages. Dreamspeakers and other native Mages would be strong in the area. Craft Masons would be extinct but some of their influence might remain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}